<title>USA: Springerville, AZ 360 MW coal unit restarting.</title>
<headline>Springerville, AZ 360 MW coal unit restarting.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 360 megawatt (MW) unit 1 at the Springerville coal-fired power plant in Arizona was restarting after being shut Saturday for tube leak repairs, sources familiar with the plant's operations said Monday.</p>
<p>The plant's other 360 MW unit was said to be operating normally.</p>
<p>The Springerville generating station is operated by Tucson Electric Power Co.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
